x=\\frac{1}{p}{e}^{px+q}+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{2}{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{2}{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}]}_{a}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[{e}^{2x}]}_{a}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot ({e}^{4}-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{e}^{2a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y={e}^{2x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{e}^{2x}=0$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{e}^{2x}=\\infty $\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047719/assets/b350aaef1440524297a84168de46be1171b7686d9937ef5bbfc5cd55835ea54f.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{2}{e}^{2x} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot ({e}^{4}-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{e}^{2a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot ({e}^{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326592 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326593 13194139535012 true] [17592186326592 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326594 13194139535012 true] [17592186326592 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326595 13194139535012 true] [17592186326592 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326596 13194139535012 true] [17592186326592 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326597 13194139535012 true] [17592186326592 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535012 true] [17592186326592 1041 "selection" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326592 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326596 13194139535012 true] [17592186326592 1110 #uuid "02b6eb07-7d70-585b-9dfb-1a3075aff8e5" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326593 1034 "The integral diverges" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326593 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535012 true] [17592186326593 1111 #uuid "9e6117bf-ea63-50eb-9123-8e2c27dc9060" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326594 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326594 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535012 true] [17592186326594 1111 #uuid "0a7be354-fc95-593c-aeb6-b44ac5239283" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326595 1034 "{e}^{2}" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326595 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535012 true] [17592186326595 1111 #uuid "036ccdc8-39a2-5db7-8d6c-02d7b53759f2" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326596 1034 "\\frac{{e}^{4}}{2}" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326596 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535012 true] [17592186326596 1111 #uuid "4902fa59-a76f-512a-a4cd-5ad55ac31b22" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326597 1034 "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326597 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535012 true] [17592186326597 1111 #uuid "2c6818f8-82f9-5c47-81ae-aa441183e5e2" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326598 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326599 13194139535012 true] [17592186326598 1089 "q-346606" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326598 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535012 true] [17592186326598 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-2}4{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326598 1113 #uuid "7e1c41ff-fb61-59f8-a754-c67ee9843025" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326598 1145 "We proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-2}4{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =4\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{-2}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[{e}^{x}]}_{a}^{-2} \\\\  & =4\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }({e}^{-2}-{e}^{a}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot (\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{e}^{a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y={e}^{x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{e}^{x}=0$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{e}^{x}=\\infty $\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047719/assets/4af4a2b7389d3773cc71e843190c6ab111355248a15e6165a8e39e37252061b9.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-2}4{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =4\\cdot (\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{e}^{a}) \\\\  & =4(\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{{e}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326599 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326600 13194139535012 true] [17592186326599 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535012 true] [17592186326599 1041 "field-1" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326599 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326600 13194139535012 true] [17592186326599 1110 #uuid "ceae2017-c078-5f16-95d5-49cf66dfe0bc" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326600 1034 "4e^{-2}" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326600 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535012 true] [17592186326600 1111 #uuid "3c6ee2fd-f367-5a9d-9011-e376d0335062" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326601 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326602 13194139535012 true] [17592186326601 1089 "q-350831" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326601 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535012 true] [17592186326601 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{-5x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326601 1113 #uuid "e02afc49-e916-5a0f-bd63-52014a86ba1c" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326601 1145 "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int {e}^{px+q}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{p}{e}^{px+q}+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{-5x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{-5x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{-5x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{-5x}]}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(-\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{-5a}+\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{5}-\\frac{1}{5}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{-5a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y={e}^{-5x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{e}^{-5x}=\\infty $\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{e}^{-5x}=0$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047719/assets/5010180e9cd41608abc630cd8974cc69ee78337bcb46a7f079d58eeb8dda9cc2.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{-5x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{5}-\\frac{1}{5}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{-5a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}(\\frac{1}{5}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326602 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326603 13194139535012 true] [17592186326602 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535012 true] [17592186326602 1041 "field-1" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326602 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326603 13194139535012 true] [17592186326602 1110 #uuid "41b070c2-84e4-5b0f-abfe-1ba3c58ce403" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326603 1034 "\\frac{3}{10}" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326603 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535012 true] [17592186326603 1111 #uuid "dd52100c-d961-5948-96c4-fedef99cf357" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326604 1034 "\\ln(4)" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326604 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535012 true] [17592186326604 1111 #uuid "6ce5ebf5-45af-590f-b079-aa0e1b5bd638" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326605 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326606 13194139535012 true] [17592186326605 1089 "q-351528" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326605 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535012 true] [17592186326605 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{3/x}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326605 1113 #uuid "875dd4ee-1f0c-53fd-8431-b98eef8a3afb" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326605 1145 "First, we substitute $u=\\frac{1}{x}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,⟹\\,-\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to -\\infty $ when $x\\to {0}^{-}$ and $u\\to 0$ when $x\\to -\\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=\\frac{1}{x}$ is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $-\\infty $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-\\infty $ | $0$ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{3/x}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{0}^{-\\infty }{e}^{3u}\\,\\text{d}u={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{e}^{3u}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{3/x}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}{e}^{3u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{{e}^{3u}}{3}]}_{a}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(1-{e}^{3a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(1-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{e}^{3a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, recall the end behavior of the function $y={e}^{3x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{e}^{3x}=0$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{e}^{3x}=\\infty $\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047719/assets/34abda46dc9fc2c6f14ce4f8460ba076a16004bb9141eb8074cdc08e0c12fd2f.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{3/x}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}(1-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{e}^{3a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326606 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326607 13194139535012 true] [17592186326606 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326608 13194139535012 true] [17592186326606 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535012 true] [17592186326606 1041 "field-1" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326606 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326608 13194139535012 true] [17592186326606 1110 #uuid "719dc9c1-bc0e-5fc4-b08e-c41f599d575f" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326607 1034 "-\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326607 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535012 true] [17592186326607 1111 #uuid "caf178c6-ee17-560f-9c52-0b174654b01b" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326608 1034 "\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326608 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535012 true] [17592186326608 1111 #uuid "6b63ef24-a739-56ad-b07f-5acb34cecd99" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326609 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326610 13194139535012 true] [17592186326609 1089 "q-351559" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326609 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535012 true] [17592186326609 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{2}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326609 1113 #uuid "e17511d0-70be-57e1-9bd3-bc3b0ce3ce74" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326609 1145 "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int {b}^{\\,px+q}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{p\\operatorname{ln}⁡(b)}{b}^{\\,px+q}+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{2}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}{2}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{{2}^{-3x}}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[{2}^{-3x}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{2}^{3a}}-\\frac{1}{{2}^{3}})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\frac{1}{{2}^{3x}},$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{1}{{2}^{3x}}=\\infty $\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{2}^{3x}}=0$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047719/assets/998ec723fd7212da4382718750465ce313349ed3f2c0258cc1f68e0a5485d968.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{2}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{2}^{3a}}-\\frac{1}{{2}^{3}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\cdot (0-\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326610 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326611 13194139535012 true] [17592186326610 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326612 13194139535012 true] [17592186326610 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535012 true] [17592186326610 1041 "field-1" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326610 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326612 13194139535012 true] [17592186326610 1110 #uuid "e5de2972-529c-5a34-816d-666268bf56f5" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326611 1034 "\\frac{1}{8\\ln(2)}" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326611 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535012 true] [17592186326611 1111 #uuid "8b08830f-a367-50a0-83be-76b3a7ff2f3c" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326612 1034 "\\frac{1}{24\\ln(2)}" 13194139535012 true] [17592186326612 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535012 true] [17592186326612 1111 #uuid "17eeab63-b8f9-5f27-8f93-ae65c815e0e2" 13194139535012 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-152232" 17592186326563 "q-152232/selection" 17592186326564 "q-152232/selection/35d8177c1ff0bff45c737e2b9568aec77f54d18fb92e3c667fbc9312c2f9d948" 17592186326565 "q-152232/selection/3be4a0b33d8ae752fcff4e19cc6abeec9ea0ac2c8234b469f7c7959c2008fb10" 17592186326566 "q-152232/selection/518e1a324b5f4439d31b4cd535c2ff871ea44859557677ae65953ab21cd53ca0" 17592186326567 "q-152232/selection/ad06fa8bb7e7